      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $y = 3x^2 - x^3$ with respect to $x$.",
        "Set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 6x - 3x^2 = 0$ and factorise.",
        "Find the corresponding $y$-coordinates for each stationary point."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $y = 3x^2 - x^3$ with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 6x - 3x^2$$",
        "Set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0$ to find the stationary $x$-values:\n$$3x(2 - x) = 0 \\implies x = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = 2$$",
        "Calculate the corresponding $y$-coordinates on the curve:\n$$\\text{At } x = 0: \\quad y = 3(0)^2 - (0)^3 = 0 \\implies (0, 0)$$\n$$\\text{At } x = 2: \\quad y = 3(2)^2 - (2)^3 = 12 - 8 = 4 \\implies (2, 4)$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
